[[2047,16,2,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>When the ignition key for the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nturned to the extreme position (AVV)[START], the solenoid winding\n(pin 50) of the starter motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied.</p><p>This supply comes from the battery via the\nline of maxifuse IGN of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>This supply is only present if there is\na safety signal - from pin 42 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               - which\nenergizes the starting enablement relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J05</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which thus supplies\npower to pin 50 of the starter motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ;   pin 76 of connector\nB of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M54</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives the starting request signal.</p><p>Pin 30 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the actual starter\nmotor, receives the voltage coming directly from the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The direct current generated by the alternator \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin B+) is sent to the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nWhen the alternator is not turning and therefore not recharging\nthe battery, an earth signal is sent from pin D+ to the rev counter module \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , pin 7 of connector B.</p><p>Module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) at pin 15 of connector A from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : when this\nsignal arrives, the &#x27;recharging&#x27; warning light comes on.</p><p>When the engine has been started up this\nsignal becomes 12 V and the warning light goes out.</p>"]]